\tag{fdip}
\title{Dual coefficients and invariant forms}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A representation and its algebraic dual can give the same
matter determinant without being isomorphic. A chosen invariant
form supplies more information: it can turn the coupled kernel
into an alternating form and force its determinant to be a
square. Which identifications and form identities establish
these two different conclusions over a coefficient ring?}

